{"parentUuid":"e2d4b173-3d56-4288-a02d-6f5669da512d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_non_blocking_error","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01QFv8hrXkCciXZtubGR5pHh","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","stderr":"Failed with non-blocking status code: /bin/sh: rtk: command not found","stdout":"","exitCode":127,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":39},"type":"attachment","uuid":"9930bfd3-269c-4431-8b90-c79d5554623f","timestamp":"2026-09-17T13:59:28.730Z","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/audit-correctness-paths","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"e2d4b173-3d56-4288-a02d-6f5669da512d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1e50a2b8-f79b-4f2b-a79b-e532971b731e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QFv8hrXkCciXZtubGR5pHh","type":"tool_result","content":"=== crates/source/s3/README.md\n116-- **Checksum** (`verify_checksum`, default `false`) — sets\n117-  `ChecksumMode::Enabled` on each `GetObject` and verifies the body against the\n118-  strongest checksum S3 has stored for the object, in order: SHA-256,\n119-  CRC-64-NVME, CRC-32C, CRC-32, then the ETag as MD5 for a non-multipart upload.\n120-  Costs a hash over the full body. If the object advertises no checksum this\n121-  source can verify, a one-shot warning is logged and the length check still\n122-  applies.\n123-\n124-Both checks operate on the **stored** bytes (below decompression), so they work\n125-unchanged for `compression`-enabled `.gz` / `.zst` objects.\n126-\n127-The two keys are the shared\n128:[`ObjectVerifySpec`](https://docs.rs/faucet-core/latest/faucet_core/verify/struct.ObjectVerifySpec.html)\n129-block, so they are named and behave identically across the S3, GCS, and Azure\n130-Blob sources (Azure exposes no body checksum and rejects `verify_checksum`).\n131-\n132-```yaml\n=== crates/source/azure-blob/README.md\n50-  **raw** stream, below any decompression, so it covers the *stored* bytes. It is\n51-  skipped, with a debug log, for a blob served with a non-empty\n52-  `Content-Encoding` (a store may transcode it on read, so the received byte\n53-  count need not match the stored size).\n54-- **Checksum** (`verify_checksum`) — **unsupported here.** Azure Blob does not\n55-  expose a body checksum (`Content-MD5`) through the `object_store` read API this\n56-  connector uses, so rather than accept a switch it cannot honour, the source\n57-  **rejects `verify_checksum: true`** at config load with a typed\n58-  `FaucetError::Config`. The `verify_length` guard above still applies. The S3\n59-  and GCS sources, whose stores do advertise a checksum, support the field.\n60-\n61-The two keys are the shared\n62:[`ObjectVerifySpec`](https://docs.rs/faucet-core/latest/faucet_core/verify/struct.ObjectVerifySpec.html)\n63-block, so they are named and behave identically across the S3, GCS, and Azure\n64-Blob sources.\n65-\n66-## File formats\n=== crates/source/gcs/README.md\n267-- **Checksum** (`verify_checksum`, default `false`) — verifies the body against\n268-  the CRC-32C (preferred) or MD5 digest GCS reports. Costs a hash over the full\n269-  body. A one-shot warning is logged if the object advertises neither.\n270-\n271-Both checks are **automatically skipped for a transcoded object** — one stored\n272-with a non-empty `Content-Encoding` (e.g. `gzip`), which GCS may decompress on\n273-read so the received bytes match neither the stored `size` nor the stored\n274-checksum. They operate on the bytes GCS delivers (below the client-side\n275-`compression` feature's decompression), so `.gz` / `.zst` objects served\n276-without a `Content-Encoding` header verify correctly.\n277-\n278-The two keys are the shared\n279:[`ObjectVerifySpec`](https://docs.rs/faucet-core/latest/faucet_core/verify/struct.ObjectVerifySpec.html)\n280-block, so they are named and behave identically across the S3, GCS, and Azure\n281-Blob sources (Azure exposes no body checksum and rejects `verify_checksum`).\n282-\n283-```yaml","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f07772a9-5efc-4757-99df-bfcd25907df3","timestamp":"2026-09-17T13:59:30.939Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== crates/source/s3/README.md\n116-- **Checksum** (`verify_checksum`, default `false`) — sets\n117-  `ChecksumMode::Enabled` on each `GetObject` and verifies the body against the\n118-  strongest checksum S3 has stored for the object, in order: SHA-256,\n119-  CRC-64-NVME, CRC-32C, CRC-32, then the ETag as MD5 for a non-multipart upload.\n120-  Costs a hash over the full body. If the object advertises no checksum this\n121-  source can verify, a one-shot warning is logged and the length check still\n122-  applies.\n123-\n124-Both checks operate on the **stored** bytes (below decompression), so they work\n125-unchanged for `compression`-enabled `.gz` / `.zst` objects.\n126-\n127-The two keys are the shared\n128:[`ObjectVerifySpec`](https://docs.rs/faucet-core/latest/faucet_core/verify/struct.ObjectVerifySpec.html)\n129-block, so they are named and behave identically across the S3, GCS, and Azure\n130-Blob sources (Azure exposes no body checksum and rejects `verify_checksum`).\n131-\n132-```yaml\n=== crates/source/azure-blob/README.md\n50-  **raw** stream, below any decompression, so it covers the *stored* bytes. It is\n51-  skipped, with a debug log, for a blob served with a non-empty\n52-  `Content-Encoding` (a store may transcode it on read, so the received byte\n53-  count need not match the stored size).\n54-- **Checksum** (`verify_checksum`) — **unsupported here.** Azure Blob does not\n55-  expose a body checksum (`Content-MD5`) through the `object_store` read API this\n56-  connector uses, so rather than accept a switch it cannot honour, the source\n57-  **rejects `verify_checksum: true`** at config load with a typed\n58-  `FaucetError::Config`. The `verify_length` guard above still applies. The S3\n59-  and GCS sources, whose stores do advertise a checksum, support the field.\n60-\n61-The two keys are the shared\n62:[`ObjectVerifySpec`](https://docs.rs/faucet-core/latest/faucet_core/verify/struct.ObjectVerifySpec.html)\n63-block, so they are named and behave identically across the S3, GCS, and Azure\n64-Blob sources.\n65-\n66-## File formats\n=== crates/source/gcs/README.md\n267-- **Checksum** (`verify_checksum`, default `false`) — verifies the body against\n268-  the CRC-32C (preferred) or MD5 digest GCS reports. Costs a hash over the full\n269-  body. A one-shot warning is logged if the object advertises neither.\n270-\n271-Both checks are **automatically skipped for a transcoded object** — one stored\n272-with a non-empty `Content-Encoding` (e.g. `gzip`), which GCS may decompress on\n273-read so the received bytes match neither the stored `size` nor the stored\n274-checksum. They operate on the bytes GCS delivers (below the client-side\n275-`compression` feature's decompression), so `.gz` / `.zst` objects served\n276-without a `Content-Encoding` header verify correctly.\n277-\n278-The two keys are the shared\n279:[`ObjectVerifySpec`](https://docs.rs/faucet-core/latest/faucet_core/verify/struct.ObjectVerifySpec.html)\n280-block, so they are named and behave identically across the S3, GCS, and Azure\n281-Blob sources (Azure exposes no body checksum and rejects `verify_checksum`).\n282-\n283-```yaml","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e2d4b173-3d56-4288-a02d-6f5669da512d","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/audit-correctness-paths","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
